    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=-\\frac52,-2,3$.",
      "worked": "Let $P(x)=2x^3+3x^2-17x-30$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(3)&=54+27-51-30\\\\P(3)&=0\\end{align*}$$\nBy the factor theorem, $x-3$ is a factor. Polynomial division gives\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=(x-3)(2x^2+9x+10)\\\\P(x)&=(x-3)(2x+5)(x+2).\\end{align*}$$\nThus $x=3,-\\frac52,-2$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
